method.description:
Converts a string identifier to the corresponding [enum ContainerForm] value. This allows using string names to identify container forms when configuring YAML styles.

[b]Example:[/b]
[codeblock]
# Convert string identifiers to ContainerForm enum values
var array_form = YAMLStyle.container_form_from_string("FORM_ARRAY")
var dict_form = YAMLStyle.container_form_from_string("FORM_DICTIONARY")

# Use these values to configure styles
var style = YAML.create_style()
style.set_container_form(array_form)

# Useful when loading style configurations from text
func apply_container_style(style, form_name):
    var form_value = YAMLStyle.container_form_from_string(form_name)
    style.set_container_form(form_value)
[/codeblock]

Converts a string identifier to the corresponding [enum FloatFormat] value. This allows using string names to identify floating-point formats when configuring YAML styles.

[b]Example:[/b]
[codeblock]
# Parse float format from configuration
var config = {
    "float_format": "FLOAT_SCIENTIFIC"
}

var style = YAML.create_style()
var format_value = YAMLStyle.float_format_from_string(config.float_format)
style.set_float_format(format_value)

# Dynamic configuration from user interface
func on_format_selected(format_name):
    var format_value = YAMLStyle.float_format_from_string(format_name)
    current_style.set_float_format(format_value)
[/codeblock]

Converts a string identifier to the corresponding [enum FlowStyle] value. This allows using string names to identify flow styles when configuring YAML styles.

[b]Example:[/b]
[codeblock]
# Load style configuration from a YAML file
var config_result = YAML.load_file("res://style_config.yaml")
if !config_result.has_error():
    var config = config_result.get_data()

    # Create style from configuration
    var style = YAML.create_style()
    if config.has("flow_style"):
        var flow_value = YAMLStyle.flow_style_from_string(config.flow_style)
        style.set_flow_style(flow_value)
[/codeblock]

Creates a new [YAMLStyle] from a [Dictionary] representation. The dictionary should contain properties and child styles in the format produced by [method to_dictionary]. Returns a new [YAMLStyle] instance with all the settings defined in the dictionary.

[b]Example:[/b]
[codeblock]
# Create a style dictionary programmatically
var style_dict = {
    "string": YAMLStyle.STRING_QUOTE_DOUBLE,
    "integer": YAMLStyle.INT_DECIMAL,
    "flow": YAMLStyle.FLOW_NONE,
    "children": {
        "inventory": {
            "flow": YAMLStyle.FLOW_SINGLE
        }
    }
}

# Convert dictionary to a YAMLStyle
var style = YAMLStyle.from_dictionary(style_dict)

# Use the style for serialization
var result = YAML.stringify(game_data, style)

# Useful for loading styles from a configuration file
func load_style_from_file(path):
    var file_result = YAML.load_file(path)
    if !file_result.has_error():
        var style_dict = file_result.get_data()
        return YAMLStyle.from_dictionary(style_dict)
    return null
[/codeblock]

Returns the child style associated with the specified [param key], or [code]null[/code] if no child style exists for this key. Use this method to access and modify child styles.

[b]Example:[/b]
[codeblock]
var style = YAML.create_style()

# Create some child styles
style.create_child("header").set_string_style(YAMLStyle.STRING_QUOTE_DOUBLE)
style.create_child("body").set_flow_style(YAMLStyle.FLOW_NONE)

# Later, retrieve and modify a child style
var header_style = style.get_child("header")
if header_style:
    header_style.set_integer_format(YAMLStyle.INT_HEX)

# Check if a child exists before using it
if style.has_child("footer"):
    var footer_style = style.get_child("footer")
    # Modify footer style...
else:
    # Create footer style if needed
    style.create_child("footer")
[/codeblock]

Returns a detailed string representation of the style configuration, including all child styles. This method is useful for debugging and inspecting the style hierarchy.

[b]Example:[/b]
[codeblock]
var style = YAML.create_style()

# Create a complex style hierarchy
style.set_string_style(YAMLStyle.STRING_QUOTE_DOUBLE)

var player_style = style.create_child("player")
player_style.set_flow_style(YAMLStyle.FLOW_NONE)

var inventory_style = player_style.create_child("inventory")
inventory_style.set_flow_style(YAMLStyle.FLOW_SINGLE)

# Print the entire style hierarchy for debugging
print("Style configuration:")
print(style.get_debug_string())

# Output might look like:
# YAMLStyle {
#   string: STRING_QUOTE_DOUBLE
#   children: {
#     player: YAMLStyle {
#       flow: FLOW_NONE
#       children: {
#         inventory: YAMLStyle {
#           flow: FLOW_SINGLE
#         }
#       }
#     }
#   }
# }
[/codeblock]

Converts a string identifier to the corresponding [enum IntegerFormat] value. This allows using string names to identify integer formats when configuring YAML styles.
[b]Example:[/b] [codeblock] # Parse format names from a configuration var settings = { "decimal_format": "INT_DECIMAL", "hex_format": "INT_HEX", "binary_format": "INT_BINARY" }
var style = YAML.create_style()
# Conditionally apply formats based on a setting var format_name = settings.hex_format var format_value = YAMLStyle.integer_format_from_string(format_name) style.set_integer_format(format_value)
print("Using format: ", format_name, " (value: ", format_value, ")") [/codeblock]
